  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Strengthening communities in habitat and risk management and climate change in Lomas de Carabayllo</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Building on the achievements of the last cycle of work, CIDAP will continue to strengthen the skills of women, men, and young people in Lomas de Carabayllo, targeting 19 communities. CIDAP will continue to focus on the food crisis, work on climate change adaptation, youth environmental leadership (with the eco-brigades), supporting 6 ollas communes, supporting human rights defenders and conservation of Lomas de Primavera, in the context of political corruption and threat posed by El Ni&#xf1;o. In addition, this project will have a new element of focus, with the work planned to reach more remote peri-urban areas of Carabayllo and helping build synergies between schools and the community to create healthy and safe environments. Cross-cutting to all these interventions, CIDAP will also provide ongoing strengthening of community organisations and their leadership.</narrative>
  </description>
